{
  "summary": "This multimodal multiprofile experiment (scvi_n200, ResNet50, avgpool aggregation, concat fusion) achieved a validation accuracy of 0.632 (F1: 0.607), a ~9.5-point improvement over the single-profile counterpart (0.536, F1: 0.516; llm_summary_005) with all other settings held constant. The result suggests that aggregating multiple profiles provides substantial additional predictive signal beyond a single profile under the established best encoder and fusion configuration, making multiprofile the most impactful design axis explored so far. It remains uncertain whether the gain is driven primarily by the multiprofile data itself, the avgpool aggregation method, or their interaction, and whether more sophisticated aggregation strategies (e.g., transformer-based) could yield further improvements on top of this new baseline."
}

